// %%
test_brain_fixture = {
  const t = liveLib.tablesOf(brainFixture);
  const strip = (id) => id.replace(/^[a-z_]+:/, "");
  const lay = (v) => { const C = relLib.compile(t, liveLib.brainSchema, v); return engine.layout({ view: C.view, nodes: C.nodes, edges: C.edges }); };
  if (t.workers.length !== 30) throw new Error("workers " + t.workers.length);
  const deploys = lay(chapters.deploys);
  if (deploys.rows.length !== 3) throw new Error("deploy steps " + deploys.rows.length);
  const cyc = lay(chapters.calls).sccs.map((s) => s.members.map(strip).join("+")).join(";");
  if (cyc !== "brain-x-fly+brain-x-loop") throw new Error("cycle " + cyc);
  const d = relLib.compile(t, liveLib.brainSchema, { boxes: ["workers"], y: [], x: [] }).report.dangling;
  const gaps = [...new Set(d.filter((g) => g.relation === "resources").map((g) => g.to))].sort().join(",");
  if (gaps !== "containers,workers") throw new Error("gaps " + gaps);
  return "fixture: 30 Workers, deploy chain 3 steps, fly ⇄ loop, gaps containers + workers";
}
// %%
test_strangers = {
  const t = liveLib.tablesOf(brainFixture);
  const reach = relLib.compile(t, liveLib.brainSchema, chapters.reach);
  if (reach.nodes.some((n) => n.id === "workers:brain-deployer")) throw new Error("a door reaches the deployer");
  const pds = reach.edges.find((e) => e.src === "actors:stranger" && e.dst === "workers:brain-x-pds");
  if (pds?.n !== 21) throw new Error("pds doors " + pds?.n);
  const abs = relLib.compile(t, liveLib.brainSchema, chapters.strangers).report.compared.filter((e) => e.state === "absence").map((e) => e.dst.slice(8)).join(",");
  if (abs !== "brain-db,brain-x-blob,brain-x-feed,brain-x-issues,brain-x-page,brain-x-pds") throw new Error("absence " + abs);
  return "no door reaches the deployer; pds has 21 doors; 6 Workers with doors and no stranger test name";
}
// %%
md`## How to read these diagrams

The same engine on a small made-up web shop, one idea per step.`
// %%
md`### 1. The data is tables

- A snapshot = a map from table name to an array of rows.
- All rows in one table have the same columns.
- Every diagram on this page, the chapters above included, is drawn from tables like these.
- The diagram reads the tables. It never changes them.`
// %%
step1_tables = htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">${Object.entries(tiny).map(([t, rows]) => htl.html`<div><strong>${t}</strong> · ${rows.length} rows${Inputs.table(rows, { rows: rows.length + 1, layout: "auto" })}</div>`)}</div>`
// %%
md`### 2. Keys make boxes and lines

- Each table names its key and which columns point at other tables.
- One \`methods\` row = one box. One \`calls\` row = one line, from \`caller\` to \`callee\`.
- A box reads columns through the pointers: a method's zone is its component's zone.
- Below: the keys, then one row per box, with the value of each level of step 4.`
// %%
step2_keys = keysView(tinySchema)
// %%
step2_result = Inputs.table(relLib.compile(tiny, tinySchema, steps.y2).nodes, { columns: ["id", "label", "zone", "zone#label", "component", "component#label"], rows: 7, layout: "auto" })
// %%
md`### 3. Y axis: one column

- View: \`y: [zone]\`. No x axis yet.
- \`zone\` is depth along \`zone_order\` of the method's \`component.zone\`: how many \`zone_order\` rows sit in front of the zone. user device = 0, public edge = 1, data store = 2. The order comes from data, not from a typed rank.
- Same value = same row. Rows are sorted by value.
- Several boxes in one row are sorted by \`id\`. Boxes never stack.`
// %%
step3 = drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.y1, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 4. Y axis: a list of columns

- View: \`y: [zone, component]\`.
- Each box gets a path. \`auth.check\` has path \`[1, "auth"]\`.
- Paths are compared left to right, like words in a dictionary.
- The left margin has one label column per level.`
// %%
step4 = drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.y2, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 5. X axis: depth along a relation

- View: \`x: [calls]\`.
- Depth = the longest chain of calls from a box that nothing calls.
- \`web.page → api.list → auth.check → db.read\`, so \`db.read\` is depth 3.
- \`db.write\` is only called by \`api.save\`, so it is depth 2.
- Only order counts. The gap between columns means nothing.
- The lines are the \`calls\` rows.`
// %%
step5 = drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.x, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 6. A cycle shares one depth

- One made-up call is added: \`auth.check → api.list\`.
- Now \`api.list\` and \`auth.check\` call each other. Neither is deeper.
- Both get the same depth. A dashed red outline marks them.`
// %%
step6 = drawTables(tinyWithCycle, tinySchema, steps.cycle, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 7. Fold: hide detail

- Click the **public edge** label in the first margin column.
- All boxes under it become one bar.
- Lines into the bar merge. **×2** = two lines merged.
- **2 inside** = lines with both ends in the bar. They are hidden.
- Folding **api** in the second column (the component) gathers only \`api.list\` and \`api.save\`. No call joins them, so there is no inside count.
- Click the bar or the label again to unfold.`
// %%
step7 = drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.fold, invalidation, { hint: "click a label in the left margin" })
// %%
md`### 8. Drag: change order by hand

- Only boxes in the same cell can swap. Try \`api.list\` and \`api.save\`.
- A drag writes rows to a separate table \`order\`: \`(id, fkey)\`. It is shown below the diagram.
- The data tables do not change.
- \`fkey\` is a text key. Boxes in a cell sort by \`fkey\`, then \`id\`.
- A new key always fits between two keys, so later drags write one row.
- Last table: example keys from \`keyBetween\`.`
// %%
step8 = drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.drag, invalidation, { hint: "drag api.save to the left of api.list" })
// %%
step8_order = {
  const rows = order[steps.drag.name] || [];
  return htl.html`<div><strong>order</strong> · ${rows.length} rows${rows.length ? Inputs.table(rows, { columns: ["id", "fkey"], layout: "auto" }) : htl.html`<div><em>empty until you drag</em></div>`}</div>`;
}
// %%
step8_keys = {
  const a = engine.keyBetween("", null), b = engine.keyBetween(a, null), m = engine.keyBetween(a, b), n = engine.keyBetween(a, m);
  return Inputs.table([
    { between: "start and end", key: a },
    { between: `${a} and end`, key: b },
    { between: `${a} and ${b}`, key: m },
    { between: `${a} and ${m}`, key: n }
  ], { layout: "auto" });
}
// %%
md`### 9. Missing values

- One method is added, \`cache.get\`. Its component has no \`zone\`.
- It cannot be placed on \`y: [zone, …]\`, so it is not drawn.
- The count is shown under the diagram.`
// %%
step9 = drawTables(tinyWithMissing, tinySchema, steps.missing, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 10. A set of boxes: hull

- A table \`flow_steps(flow, step, method)\` lists the methods one save request passes through.
- The view names the foreign key \`flow_steps.method\` and the column \`flow\`: one hull per flow, around the boxes its rows name.
- One outline is drawn around each hull's boxes.
- The outline is convex, so it can cover a box that is not in the set (\`api.list\` here).`
// %%
step10 = drawTables(tinyWithHull, tinySchema, steps.hull, invalidation)
// %%
md`### 11. Same data, two views

- First view: y = trust zone. Second view: y = compute (where the code runs).
- \`auth\` and \`database\` are in different zones but both run serverless.
- Fold **serverless** in the second view. The first does not change: each view has its own folds.
- Hover a box. The same row is outlined orange in both views.`
// %%
step11 = htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">${drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.byZone, invalidation)}${drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.byCompute, invalidation)}</div>`
// %%
step12 = htl.html`<div>${md`### 12. Y axis from a relation

- View: \`y: [calls]\`, \`x: [zone]\`. Step 5 turned around.
- Any edge relation works on either axis.
- Why it is allowed:
  - a relation = a directed graph
  - "a reaches b" is a preorder (reflexive, transitive)
  - a cycle breaks antisymmetry, so merge each cycle into one node (step 6)
  - the merged graph is a POSET
  - a POSET is not a line, so pick a rank: longest path from a source
- Same rank does not mean related. \`auth.check\` and \`db.write\` are both depth 2 and never call each other.
- So folding **depth 2** gathers boxes that only share a number. Relation levels are good for position, column levels for grouping.`}
${drawTables(tiny, tinySchema, steps.yRel, invalidation, { hint: "click depth 2 in the left margin" })}
${md`### 13. The design against the calls

- The shop's design doc is one more table, \`intended\`: component → component, marked docs.
- View: \`compare: [{ claimed: "intended", observed: "calls" }]\`. Calls lift to their components, then each pair of components gets one line.
- grey \`web → api\`, \`api → db\`, \`auth → db\`: in the doc and in the calls.
- orange \`api → auth\`: two calls the doc does not mention. Hover it to see them.
- red dashed \`web → auth\`: in the doc, never called.
- A line is wider the more rows are behind it. Folding sums those rows, so a fold's ×n counts calls, not lines.`}
${drawTables(tinyWithIntent, tinySchema, steps.compare, invalidation)}
${md`### Summary

- data: tables with keys, never edited
- view: which tables are boxes, which relations are lines, + a list of levels per axis
- level: a column, also through a foreign key (sorted by value), or depth along a relation
- tie break: \`order\` table key, then \`id\`
- relation level: cycles merged, then rank = longest path. Good to place, weak to fold
- fold: a y label becomes one bar; lines merge, ×n counts the rows behind them
- compare: a claimed relation against an observed one, one line per pair of ends
- several views over one snapshot, each with its own folds and order`}</div>`
// %%
tinyLib = {
// A small made-up web shop, used by the step-by-step part of the notebook.
const tiny = {
  zones: [
    { id: "device", name: "user device" },
    { id: "edge", name: "public edge" },
    { id: "data", name: "data store" }
  ],
  // outer_zone is in front of inner_zone, as seen from the user.
  zone_order: [
    { outer_zone: "device", inner_zone: "edge" },
    { outer_zone: "edge", inner_zone: "data" }
  ],
  components: [
    { id: "web", name: "web app", zone: "device", compute: "browser", compute_rank: 0 },
    { id: "api", name: "api", zone: "edge", compute: "container", compute_rank: 1 },
    { id: "auth", name: "auth", zone: "edge", compute: "serverless", compute_rank: 2 },
    { id: "db", name: "database", zone: "data", compute: "serverless", compute_rank: 2 }
  ],
  methods: [
    { id: "web.page", component: "web" },
    { id: "api.list", component: "api" },
    { id: "api.save", component: "api" },
    { id: "auth.check", component: "auth" },
    { id: "db.read", component: "db" },
    { id: "db.write", component: "db" }
  ],
  calls: [
    { caller: "web.page", callee: "api.list" },
    { caller: "web.page", callee: "api.save" },
    { caller: "api.list", callee: "auth.check" },
    { caller: "api.save", callee: "auth.check" },
    { caller: "api.list", callee: "db.read" },
    { caller: "api.save", callee: "db.write" },
    { caller: "auth.check", callee: "db.read" }
  ]
};

// Variants for single steps.
const tinyWithHull = {
  ...tiny,
  flow_steps: [
    { flow: "save request", step: 1, method: "web.page" },
    { flow: "save request", step: 2, method: "api.save" },
    { flow: "save request", step: 3, method: "auth.check" },
    { flow: "save request", step: 4, method: "db.write" }
  ]
};
const tinyWithCycle = { ...tiny, calls: [...tiny.calls, { caller: "auth.check", callee: "api.list" }] };
// What the shop's design doc says each component calls. It leaves out api → auth and claims web → auth.
const tinyWithIntent = {
  ...tiny,
  intended: [
    { from: "web", to: "api" },
    { from: "web", to: "auth" },
    { from: "api", to: "db" },
    { from: "auth", to: "db" }
  ]
};
const tinyWithMissing = {
  ...tiny,
  components: [...tiny.components, { id: "cache", name: "cache", zone: null, compute: null, compute_rank: null }],
  methods: [...tiny.methods, { id: "cache.get", component: "cache" }]
};


// The shop's keys, for drawing its tables directly (rel.js).
const tinySchema = {
  tables: {
    zones: { key: "id", label: "name" },
    zone_order: { link: ["outer_zone", "inner_zone"], refs: { outer_zone: "zones", inner_zone: "zones" } },
    components: { key: "id", label: "name", refs: { zone: "zones" } },
    methods: { key: "id", refs: { component: "components" } },
    calls: { link: ["caller", "callee"], refs: { caller: "methods", callee: "methods" } },
    flow_steps: { key: ["flow", "step"], refs: { method: "methods" } },
    intended: { link: ["from", "to"], refs: { from: "components", to: "components" }, prov: "docs" }
  }
};

// The tutorial's views. A box is a methods row; a line is a calls row.
const zone = { name: "zone", depth: "zone_order", at: "component.zone", label: "name" };
const component = { name: "component", col: "component", label: "component.name" };
const compute = { name: "compute", col: "component.compute_rank", label: "component.compute" };
const calls = { depth: "calls" };
const shop = { boxes: ["methods"], lines: ["calls"] };
const steps = {
  y1: { name: "step: y = zone", ...shop, lines: [], y: [zone], x: [], xTitle: "" },
  y2: { name: "step: y = zone, component", ...shop, lines: [], y: [zone, component], x: [], xTitle: "" },
  x: { name: "step: x = depth along calls", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  cycle: { name: "step: a cycle", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  fold: { name: "step: fold", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  drag: { name: "step: drag", ...shop, y: [zone], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  missing: { name: "step: missing value", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  hull: { name: "step: hull", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth", hulls: [{ relation: "flow_steps.method", by: "flow" }] },
  compare: { name: "step: the design against the calls", boxes: ["components"], nest: ["methods.component"], lines: [], compare: [{ claimed: "intended", observed: "calls" }], y: [{ name: "zone", depth: "zone_order", at: "zone", label: "name" }], x: [], xTitle: "", wrap: 4 },
  yRel: { name: "step: y = depth along calls", ...shop, y: [calls], x: [zone], xTitle: "zone", yTitle: "depth" },
  byZone: { name: "by trust zone", ...shop, y: [zone, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" },
  byCompute: { name: "by compute", ...shop, y: [compute, component], x: [calls], xTitle: "depth" }
};
  return { tiny, tinyWithHull, tinyWithCycle, tinyWithMissing, tinyWithIntent, steps, tinySchema };
}
// %%
tiny = tinyLib.tiny
// %%
tinyWithHull = tinyLib.tinyWithHull
// %%
tinyWithCycle = tinyLib.tinyWithCycle
// %%
tinyWithMissing = tinyLib.tinyWithMissing
// %%
tinyWithIntent = tinyLib.tinyWithIntent
// %%
tinySchema = tinyLib.tinySchema
// %%
steps = tinyLib.steps
// %%
test_hull = {
  const C = relLib.compile(tinyWithHull, tinySchema, steps.hull);
  const L = engine.layout({ view: C.view, nodes: C.nodes, edges: C.edges, hulls: C.hulls });
  const h = L.hulls.map((x) => x.hull + ": " + x.items.map((id) => id.replace(/^methods:/, "")).join(",")).join("; ");
  if (h !== "save request: api.save,auth.check,db.write,web.page") throw new Error("hulls " + h);
  return h;
}
// %%
test_compare = {
  const C = relLib.compile(tinyWithIntent, tinySchema, steps.compare);
  const got = C.edges.map((e) => `${e.state} ${e.src.slice(11)}→${e.dst.slice(11)}`).join("; ");
  if (got !== "divergence api→auth; convergence api→db; convergence auth→db; convergence web→api; absence web→auth") throw new Error("compare " + got);
  const k = relLib.compile(liveLib.tablesOf(brainFixture), brainSchema, chapters.claims).report.compared.map((e) => `${e.state} ${e.src.slice(8)}→${e.dst.slice(8)}`).join("; ");
  if (k !== "absence brain→brain-deployer") throw new Error("cb4 claims " + k);
  return got + "; cb4: " + k;
}
// %%
test_tutorial_steps = {
  const lay = (data, v, folds = []) => { const C = relLib.compile(data, tinySchema, v); return engine.layout({ view: C.view, nodes: C.nodes, edges: C.edges, folds }); };
  const bare = (ids) => ids.map((id) => id.replace(/^methods:/, "")).join(",");
  const X = lay(tiny, steps.x);
  const colOf = (id) => X.items.find((it) => it.id === "methods:" + id).col;
  const depths = ["web.page", "api.list", "auth.check", "db.write", "db.read"].map(colOf).join(",");
  if (depths !== "0,1,2,2,3") throw new Error("depths " + depths);
  const cyc = lay(tinyWithCycle, steps.cycle).sccs.map((c) => `${c.relation}: ${bare(c.members)}`).join("; ");
  if (cyc !== "calls: api.list,auth.check") throw new Error("cycle " + cyc);
  const m = bare(lay(tiny, steps.byCompute, [[2]]).items.find((it) => it.kind === "group").members);
  if (m !== "auth.check,db.read,db.write") throw new Error("serverless fold " + m);
  const y2 = bare(lay(tiny, steps.yRel, [[2]]).items.find((it) => it.kind === "group").members);
  if (y2 !== "auth.check,db.write") throw new Error("depth 2 fold " + y2);
  return "depths 0,1,2,2,3; cycle api.list+auth.check; serverless folds auth.check, db.read, db.write; y depth 2 folds auth.check, db.write";
}
// %%
md`### Machinery

The cells below are shared by every diagram above.`
// %%
// Levels offered: every column of every table, each column one foreign key out, and depth along each relation.
tableOptions = {
  const { tables, schema } = tableSets[tableSet];
  const S = schema.tables, rels = relLib.relationsOf(schema);
  const cols = (t) => [...new Set((tables[t] || []).flatMap((r) => Object.keys(r)))].filter((c) => c !== S[t].href);
  // A foreign key into several tables is offered as a column but not followed.
  const one = (r) => (Array.isArray(r) ? undefined : r);
  const refs = (t) => Object.entries(S[t].refs || {}).filter(([, to]) => one(to));
  const labelOf = (t) => S[t].label || (Array.isArray(S[t].key) ? null : S[t].key);
  const levels = { table: { table: true } };
  for (const t of Object.keys(S).filter((t) => !S[t].link)) {
    for (const c of cols(t)) {
      const to = one((S[t].refs || {})[c]);
      // A box already has an id, label, kind and href, so a level on one of those columns needs its own name.
      const named = ["id", "label", "kind", "href"].includes(c) ? { name: `row ${c}` } : {};
      levels[c] ??= to && labelOf(to) ? { ...named, col: c, label: `${c}.${labelOf(to)}` } : { ...named, col: c };
    }
    for (const [c, to] of refs(t)) for (const d of cols(to)) {
      const path = `${c}.${d}`, to2 = one((S[to].refs || {})[d]);
      levels[path] ??= to2 && labelOf(to2) ? { col: path, label: `${path}.${labelOf(to2)}` } : { col: path };
      for (const r of rels.filter((r) => to2 && r.fromTables.join() === to2 && r.toTables.join() === to2)) levels[`depth along ${r.name} of ${path}`] = { depth: r.name, at: path, label: labelOf(to2) };
    }
  }
  for (const r of rels) levels[`depth along ${r.name}`] = { depth: r.name };
  levels["nest 1"] = { nest: 1 };
  return {
    relations: rels.map((r) => r.name),
    foreignKeys: rels.filter((r) => !r.from).map((r) => r.name),
    columns: Object.keys(levels).filter((k) => levels[k].col && !levels[k].name).sort(),
    levels: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(levels).sort(([a], [b]) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0)))
  };
}
// %%
tableSets = ({
  cb4: {
    tables: brainTables, schema: liveLib.brainSchema,
    defaults: { boxes: ["methods", "workers"], lines: ["calls"], nest: ["methods.worker"], y: ["role", "nest 1"], x: ["depth along calls"] }
  },
  "web shop": {
    tables: tinyLib.tinyWithHull, schema: tinyLib.tinySchema,
    defaults: { boxes: ["methods"], lines: ["calls"], nest: ["methods.component"], y: ["depth along zone_order of component.zone", "nest 1"], x: ["depth along calls"] }
  }
})
// %%
// A chain of selects, outermost first. The last one reads "none"; picking a value there adds a slot,
// and setting any slot to "none" removes it, so the ones after it move up.
levelList = (options, label, init) => {
  let levels = [...init];
  const root = htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:4px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:3px 0"><span style="width:110px">${label}</span></div>`;
  const list = htl.html`<span style="display:contents"></span>`;
  root.append(list);
  const draw = () => list.replaceChildren(...[...levels, "none"].map((v, i) => {
    const sel = htl.html`<select>${["none", ...options].map((o) => htl.html`<option selected=${o === v}>${o}</option>`)}</select>`;
    sel.oninput = () => {
      if (sel.value === "none") levels.splice(i, 1);
      else levels[i] = sel.value;
      draw();
    };
    return htl.html`<span>${i ? "› " : ""}${sel}</span>`;
  }));
  Object.defineProperty(root, "value", { get: () => [...levels], set: (v) => { levels = [...v]; draw(); } });
  draw();
  return root;
}
// %%
relLib = {
  const { posetRanks } = engine;
// Draw any set of tables. A box is a row, a line is a relation, a level is an expression on a row.
// compile() turns tables + a key schema + a view into the rows the layout engine reads. Pure and sorted.
//
// schema.tables[name]: { key?: col | [cols], label?: col, href?: col, refs?: { col: table | [tables] }, link?: [fromCol, toCol], prov? }
//   A relation is a foreign key, named "table.col", or a link table, named "table" (one line per row, from link[0] to link[1]).
//   A foreign key naming several tables points at the first of them holding the key.
//   prov ("data" unless given) is where a table's rows come from; a line is "docs" if its table or a row it was lifted through is.
// view: { boxes: [table], lines: [relation], nest: [foreign key], y: [level], x: [level], where?: { level or path: [values] },
//   compare?: [{ claimed: relation, observed: relation, scope?: "claimed" }] (one line per pair of drawn ends, marked convergence, divergence or absence;
//     scope "claimed" keeps only the divergences that end at a box a claim ends at),
//   show?: [path], connected?: [table] (rows of these tables are boxes only when a drawn line ends at them), hulls?: [{ relation: foreign key, by: col }] (one outline per value of by, around the rows the key names),
//   ...passed to the engine: name, wrap, cards, edgeLabels, slot, xTitle, yTitle, folds }
// level: { col: "path", label?: "path" }   a column, read through foreign keys ("component.zone");
//                                           a nested row without the column reads it from its parent
//        { depth: relation, at?: "path", label?: "path" }  depth along a relation; with at, the depth of the row that path reaches
//        { nest: k }                        the ancestor k steps below the nest root (1 = the root)
//        { table: true }                    the row's table


const cmp = (a, b) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);
const isNil = (v) => v === null || v === undefined;
const list = (v) => (isNil(v) ? [] : [].concat(v));

const levelName = (l) => l.name || (l.table ? "table" : l.nest ? `nest ${l.nest}` : l.depth ? `depth along ${l.depth}${l.at ? ` of ${l.at}` : ""}` : l.col);

const relationsOf = (schema) => Object.entries(schema.tables).flatMap(([t, s]) => [
  ...(s.link ? [{ name: t, table: t, from: s.link[0], to: s.link[1], fromTables: list(s.refs[s.link[0]]), toTables: list(s.refs[s.link[1]]) }] : []),
  ...Object.entries(s.refs || {}).filter(([c]) => !(s.link || []).includes(c)).map(([c, to]) => ({ name: `${t}.${c}`, table: t, from: null, to: c, fromTables: [t], toTables: list(to) }))
]).sort((a, b) => cmp(a.name, b.name));

const compile = (tables, schema, view) => {
  const S = schema.tables;
  const keyOf = (t, row, i) => { const k = S[t].key; return isNil(k) ? String(i) : Array.isArray(k) ? k.map((c) => row[c]).join("/") : String(row[k]); };
  const rowsOf = (t) => [...(tables[t] || [])].map((row, i) => ({ row, k: keyOf(t, row, i) })).sort((a, b) => cmp(a.k, b.k));
  const index = new Map(Object.keys(S).sort().map((t) => [t, new Map(rowsOf(t).map(({ row, k }) => [k, row]))]));
  const find = (t, k) => (isNil(k) || !index.has(t) ? undefined : index.get(t).get(String(k)));
  // The row a key names in the first of the tables that holds it.
  const findIn = (ts, k) => { for (const t of ts) { const row = find(t, k); if (row) return { t, row }; } return null; };
  const refsOf = (t, c) => list((S[t].refs || {})[c]);
  const id = (t, row) => `${t}:${keyOf(t, row)}`;
  const dangling = [];

  // Nesting: each nested table has one foreign key to its parent.
  const nestCol = new Map((view.nest || []).map((r) => { const [t, c] = r.split("."); return [t, c]; }));
  const parentOf = (t, row) => {
    const c = nestCol.get(t);
    if (!c) return null;
    return findIn(refsOf(t, c), row[c]);
  };
  const chain = (t, row) => { const out = [{ t, row }]; for (let p = parentOf(t, row); p; p = parentOf(p.t, p.row)) out.unshift(p); return out; };

  // A path walks foreign keys; a column a row lacks is read from its nest parent.
  const get = (t, row, path) => {
    if (!row) return { value: null };
    const [c, ...rest] = path;
    if (!rest.length) {
      if (c in row) return { value: row[c], t, row };
      const p = parentOf(t, row);
      return p ? get(p.t, p.row, path) : { value: null };
    }
    const to = refsOf(t, c);
    if (to.length && c in row) { const r = findIn(to, row[c]); return r ? get(r.t, r.row, rest) : { value: null }; }
    const p = parentOf(t, row);
    return p ? get(p.t, p.row, path) : { value: null };
  };
  // The row a path of foreign keys reaches.
  const reach = (t, row, path) => {
    if (!path) return { t, row };
    const segs = path.split(".");
    let cur = { t, row };
    for (const c of segs) {
      while (cur.row && !(c in cur.row)) { const p = parentOf(cur.t, cur.row); if (!p) return null; cur = p; }
      if (!cur.row) return null;
      const r = findIn(refsOf(cur.t, c), cur.row[c]);
      if (!r) return null;
      cur = r;
    }
    return cur;
  };

  const relations = new Map(relationsOf(schema).map((r) => [r.name, r]));
  const pairsMemo = new Map();
  const pairsOf = (name) => {
    if (!pairsMemo.has(name)) pairsMemo.set(name, pairsFor(name));
    return pairsMemo.get(name);
  };
  const pairsFor = (name) => {
    const r = relations.get(name);
    if (!r) throw new Error(`no relation ${name}`);
    return rowsOf(r.table).flatMap(({ row }) => {
      const a = r.from ? findIn(r.fromTables, row[r.from]) : { t: r.table, row };
      const b = findIn(r.toTables, row[r.to]);
      if (!a || !b) {
        if (!isNil(row[r.to]) || r.from) dangling.push({ relation: name, from: r.from ? row[r.from] : keyOf(r.table, row), to: row[r.to] });
        return [];
      }
      return [{ a, b, prov: S[r.table].prov || "data" }];
    });
  };

  // Depth of rows of one table along a relation, for depth levels with at.
  const depthAt = new Map();
  const depthOf = (rel, t, row) => {
    const k = rel + "\u0000" + t;
    if (!depthAt.has(k)) {
      const pairs = pairsOf(rel).filter((p) => p.a.t === t && p.b.t === t).map((p) => ({ src: keyOf(t, p.a.row), dst: keyOf(t, p.b.row) }));
      depthAt.set(k, posetRanks(rowsOf(t).map((r) => r.k), pairs).rank);
    }
    return depthAt.get(k).get(keyOf(t, row));
  };

  const levels = [...(view.y || []), ...(view.x || [])];
  const valueOf = (l, t, row) => {
    if (l.table) return { value: t };
    if (l.nest) { const c = chain(t, row); const a = c[l.nest - 1] || null; return a ? { value: id(a.t, a.row), label: String(a.row[S[a.t].label] ?? keyOf(a.t, a.row)) } : { value: null }; }
    if (l.depth && l.at) {
      const r = reach(t, row, l.at);
      if (!r) return { value: null };
      return { value: depthOf(l.depth, r.t, r.row), label: l.label ? get(r.t, r.row, l.label.split(".")).value : undefined };
    }
    if (l.col) {
      const v = get(t, row, l.col.split(".")).value;
      return { value: isNil(v) ? null : v, label: l.label ? get(t, row, l.label.split(".")).value : undefined };
    }
    return { value: null };
  };

  const boxes = new Set(view.boxes);
  const str = (v) => (isNil(v) ? "∅" : String(v));
  const where = Object.entries(view.where || {}).map(([k, vs]) => [k, new Set(vs.map(String))]);
  const byName = new Map(levels.map((l) => [levelName(l), l]));
  // A level is stored on the box under its name, so it cannot take a name the box already uses.
  for (const name of [...byName.keys(), ...(view.show || [])]) if (["id", "label", "kind", "href"].includes(name)) throw new Error(`a level or show path named "${name}" would replace the box's own ${name}; give the level a name`);
  const nodes = [], drawn = new Map();
  for (const t of [...boxes].sort()) for (const { row } of rowsOf(t)) {
    const n = { id: id(t, row), label: String(row[S[t].label] ?? keyOf(t, row)), kind: t, href: S[t].href ? row[S[t].href] ?? null : null };
    const c = chain(t, row);
    n["#root"] = id(c[0].t, c[0].row);
    n["#depth"] = c.length - 1;
    for (const l of levels) if (!(l.depth && !l.at)) {
      const v = valueOf(l, t, row), name = levelName(l);
      n[name] = v.value;
      if (v.label !== undefined) n[name + "#label"] = v.label;
    }
    for (const p of view.show || []) n[p] = get(t, row, p.split(".")).value;
    const ok = where.every(([k, vs]) => vs.has(str(byName.has(k) ? n[k] : get(t, row, k.split(".")).value)));
    if (!ok) continue;
    nodes.push(n);
    drawn.set(n.id, n);
  }

  // A line to a row that is not drawn goes to its nearest drawn nest ancestor, and is "docs" if it passed a docs row.
  const drawnOf = (e) => {
    let prov = "data";
    for (const a of [...chain(e.t, e.row)].reverse()) {
      const k = id(a.t, a.row);
      if (drawn.has(k)) return { id: k, prov };
      if (boxes.has(a.t)) return null;
      if (S[a.t].prov === "docs") prov = "docs";
    }
    return null;
  };
  // Lines with the same drawn ends, relation and source are one line, labelled with the keys they end at.
  // Each line keeps the base rows behind it: n of them, as "from → to" keys.
  const compares = view.compare || [];
  const rels = [...new Set([...(view.lines || []), ...compares.flatMap((c) => [c.claimed, c.observed]), ...levels.filter((l) => l.depth && !l.at).map((l) => l.depth)])].sort();
  const lineMap = new Map(), inside = {};
  let hidden = 0;
  for (const rel of rels) for (const p of pairsOf(rel)) {
    const s = drawnOf(p.a), d = drawnOf(p.b);
    if (!s || !d) { hidden++; continue; }
    if (s.id === d.id) { inside[rel] = (inside[rel] || 0) + 1; continue; }
    const prov = [p.prov, s.prov, d.prov].includes("docs") ? "docs" : p.prov;
    const k = [s.id, d.id, rel, prov].join("\u0000");
    if (!lineMap.has(k)) lineMap.set(k, { src: s.id, dst: d.id, rel, prov, label: new Set(), pairs: new Set() });
    const e = lineMap.get(k);
    e.label.add(keyOf(p.b.t, p.b.row));
    e.pairs.add(`${keyOf(p.a.t, p.a.row)} → ${keyOf(p.b.t, p.b.row)}`);
  }
  const done = (e) => ({ ...e, label: [...e.label].sort(cmp), pairs: [...e.pairs].sort(cmp), n: e.pairs.size });
  let edges = [...lineMap.keys()].sort().map((k) => done(lineMap.get(k)));
  // A reflexion model (Murphy, Notkin, Sullivan 1995): the claimed lines against the observed ones, on the drawn ends.
  const compared = [];
  for (const c of compares) {
    const name = `${c.observed} against ${c.claimed}`, ends = new Map();
    for (const e of edges) for (const side of ["claimed", "observed"]) if (e.rel === c[side]) {
      const k = e.src + "\u0000" + e.dst;
      if (!ends.has(k)) ends.set(k, { src: e.src, dst: e.dst, claimed: [], observed: [] });
      ends.get(k)[side].push(e);
    }
    const claimedDst = new Set([...ends.values()].filter((x) => x.claimed.length).map((x) => x.dst));
    for (const x of [...ends.values()]) {
      const state = x.claimed.length && x.observed.length ? "convergence" : x.observed.length ? "divergence" : "absence";
      if (state === "divergence" && c.scope === "claimed" && !claimedDst.has(x.dst)) continue;
      const of = state === "absence" ? x.claimed : x.observed, all = [...x.claimed, ...x.observed];
      compared.push({
        src: x.src, dst: x.dst, rel: name, state, prov: of.some((e) => e.prov === "docs") ? "docs" : "data",
        label: [...new Set(all.flatMap((e) => e.label))].sort(cmp), pairs: [...new Set(all.flatMap((e) => e.pairs))].sort(cmp), n: of.reduce((t, e) => t + e.n, 0),
        claimed: [...new Set(x.claimed.flatMap((e) => e.pairs))].sort(cmp), observed: [...new Set(x.observed.flatMap((e) => e.pairs))].sort(cmp)
      });
    }
  }
  const comparedRels = new Set(compares.flatMap((c) => [c.claimed, c.observed]));
  if (compares.length) edges = [...edges.filter((e) => !comparedRels.has(e.rel) || (view.lines || []).includes(e.rel) || levels.some((l) => l.depth === e.rel && !l.at)), ...compared.map(({ claimed: _a, observed: _b, ...e }) => e)]
    .sort((a, b) => cmp(a.src, b.src) || cmp(a.dst, b.dst) || cmp(a.rel, b.rel));
  const connected = new Set(view.connected || []);
  if (connected.size) {
    const ends = new Set(edges.flatMap((e) => [e.src, e.dst]));
    for (let i = nodes.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (connected.has(nodes[i].kind) && !ends.has(nodes[i].id)) nodes.splice(i, 1);
  }
  const hulls = (view.hulls || []).flatMap((h) => pairsOf(h.relation).map((p) => ({ hull: String(p.a.row[h.by]), d: drawnOf(p.b) })).filter((x) => x.d).map((x) => ({ hull: x.hull, id: x.d.id })));

  // Every relation is resolved for the report, drawn or not: a key that names no row is a gap in the data.
  for (const r of relations.keys()) pairsOf(r);
  const nested = (view.nest || []).length > 0;
  const toEngine = (l) => {
    const name = levelName(l);
    if (l.depth && !l.at) return { relation: l.depth, ...(nested ? { by: "#root" } : {}) };
    const hasLabel = l.nest || l.label;
    return { col: name, ...(hasLabel ? { label: name + "#label" } : {}) };
  };
  const { boxes: _b, lines, nest, y, x, where: _w, hulls: _h, connected: _c, compare: _k, ...pass } = view;
  return {
    nodes, edges, hulls,
    view: { ...pass, y: (y || []).map(toEngine), x: (x || []).map(toEngine), drawRelations: [...(lines || []), ...compares.map((c) => `${c.observed} against ${c.claimed}`)], cellSort: ["#depth", ...(pass.cellSort || [])] },
    report: { dangling: dangling.sort((a, b) => cmp(a.relation, b.relation) || cmp(String(a.from), String(b.from)) || cmp(String(a.to), String(b.to))), hidden, inside, compared }
  };
};
  return { compile, relationsOf, levelName };
}
// %%
// Compiles a view over tables and draws it. With gaps, keys that name no row are listed under it.
drawTables = (tables, schema, view, invalidation, { gaps, ...opts } = {}) => {
  const C = relLib.compile(tables, schema, view);
  const host = diagramFor(C.view, invalidation, C, opts);
  const d = C.report.dangling;
  if (gaps && d.length) host.append(htl.html`<details style="margin-top:6px"><summary>${d.length} keys name no row</summary><ul>${d.map((g) => htl.html`<li><code>${g.relation}</code>: ${g.from} → <code>${g.to}</code></li>`)}</ul></details>`);
  return host;
}
// %%
// A schema's tables, one line each: key, label, foreign keys, link.
keysView = (schema) => htl.html`<pre style="font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap">${Object.entries(schema.tables).map(([t, d]) => `${t}: ${JSON.stringify(d)}`).join("\n")}</pre>`
// %%
viewof folds = Inputs.input({})
// %%
viewof order = Inputs.input({})
// %%
// Label of a prefix of column levels: the label column of the first row (by id) under it.
axisLabel = (rows, levels, title) => (prefix) => {
  if (!prefix.length) return title;
  const k = prefix.length - 1, lvl = levels[k];
  if (levels.slice(0, k + 1).some((l) => !l.col)) return `${title} ${prefix.join(" · ")}`;
  const hit = [...rows.nodes].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : 1)).find((n) => levels.slice(0, k + 1).every((l, i) => n[l.col] === prefix[i]));
  return hit && lvl.label ? String(hit[lvl.label]) : String(prefix[k]);
}
// %%
focusBus = new EventTarget()
// %%
diagramFor = (v, invalidation, rows, { hint } = {}) => {
  const myFolds = folds[v.name] ?? v.folds ?? [], myOrder = order[v.name] || [];
  const L = engine.layout({ view: v, ...rows, order: myOrder, folds: myFolds });
  const { svg, geometry } = engine.render(L, { labelFor: axisLabel(rows, v.y, v.yTitle || ""), xLabelFor: axisLabel(rows, v.x, v.xTitle) });
  const host = htl.html`<div style="background:#f6f7f9;color:#111827;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;overflow-x:auto;font:12px system-ui"><div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">${v.name}</div></div>`;
  const pic = htl.html`<div></div>`;
  pic.innerHTML = svg;
  host.append(pic);
  const name = new Map(rows.nodes.map((n) => [n.id, n.label ?? n.id]));
  const notes = [hint, L.excluded.length && `${L.excluded.length} ${L.excluded.length === 1 ? "row has" : "rows have"} no value for this view's axes and ${L.excluded.length === 1 ? "is" : "are"} not drawn (${L.excluded.map((id) => name.get(id)).join(", ")})`].filter(Boolean);
  if (notes.length) host.append(htl.html`<div style="margin-top:6px;opacity:.75">${notes.join(" · ")}</div>`);
  const setInput = (input, value) => { input.value = value; input.dispatchEvent(new window.Event("input", { bubbles: true })); };
  const cellOf = new Map();
  for (const ids of L.cells.values()) for (const id of ids) cellOf.set(id, ids);
  pic.querySelectorAll(".odg-scc").forEach((el) => {
    const t = window.document.createElementNS("http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "title");
    t.textContent = `these rows reach each other along ${el.getAttribute("data-relation")}, so they share a rank`;
    el.append(t);
  });
  // data-fold is a prefix (one band or bar) or a level number (every prefix of that length).
  pic.querySelectorAll("[data-fold]").forEach((el) => el.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const f = JSON.parse(el.getAttribute("data-fold"));
    const same = (a) => (b) => JSON.stringify(b) === JSON.stringify(a);
    const has = (x) => myFolds.some(same(x));
    const drop = (x) => myFolds.filter((y) => !same(x)(y));
    let next;
    if (!Array.isArray(f)) next = has(f) ? drop(f).filter((y) => !(y && y.open && y.open.length === f)) : [...myFolds.filter((y) => !(Array.isArray(y) && y.length === f)), f];
    else if (has(f)) next = drop(f);
    else if (has(f.length) && has({ open: f })) next = drop({ open: f });
    else if (has(f.length)) next = [...myFolds, { open: f }];
    else next = [...myFolds, f];
    setInput(viewof folds, { ...folds, [v.name]: next });
  }));
  // Linked hover: every view highlights the boxes holding any of the hovered ids.
  const idsOf = (el) => (el.getAttribute("data-id") || el.getAttribute("data-members") || "").split(" ").filter(Boolean);
  pic.querySelectorAll(".odg-node, .odg-group").forEach((el) => {
    el.addEventListener("pointerenter", () => focusBus.dispatchEvent(new window.CustomEvent("focus", { detail: idsOf(el) })));
    el.addEventListener("pointerleave", () => focusBus.dispatchEvent(new window.CustomEvent("focus", { detail: [] })));
  });
  const onFocus = (e) => {
    const want = new Set(e.detail);
    pic.querySelectorAll(".odg-node, .odg-group").forEach((el) => {
      const r = el.querySelector("rect");
      const hit = want.size && idsOf(el).some((id) => want.has(id));
      r.setAttribute("stroke-width", hit ? "3" : "1");
      r.setAttribute("stroke", hit ? "#f97316" : el.classList.contains("odg-group") ? "#3b82f6" : "#9ca3af");
    });
  };
  focusBus.addEventListener("focus", onFocus);
  invalidation.then(() => focusBus.removeEventListener("focus", onFocus));
  pic.querySelectorAll(".odg-node").forEach((el) => el.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => {
    if (e.target.closest(".odg-link")) return;
    const id = el.getAttribute("data-id");
    const ids = cellOf.get(id);
    if (!ids || ids.length < 2) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    el.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
    const svgEl = pic.querySelector("svg");
    const scale = svgEl.viewBox.baseVal.width / svgEl.getBoundingClientRect().width;
    const x0 = e.clientX;
    let dx = 0;
    const move = (m) => { dx = (m.clientX - x0) * scale; el.setAttribute("transform", `translate(${dx},0)`); };
    const done = () => {
      el.removeEventListener("pointermove", move);
      el.removeEventListener("pointerup", up);
      el.removeEventListener("pointercancel", cancel);
    };
    const cancel = () => { done(); el.removeAttribute("transform"); };
    const up = () => {
      done();
      // Reading order inside a wrapped cell: line first, then x.
      const at = (k) => { const b = geometry.box.get(k); return [b.y, b.x + b.w / 2]; };
      const [myY, myX] = at(id);
      const before = ([y, x]) => y < myY || (y === myY && x < myX + dx);
      const toIndex = ids.filter((o) => o !== id && before(at(o))).length;
      if (toIndex === ids.indexOf(id)) { el.removeAttribute("transform"); return; }
      const res = engine.reorder({ order: myOrder, cellIds: ids, id, toIndex });
      setInput(viewof order, { ...order, [v.name]: res.order });
    };
    el.addEventListener("pointermove", move);
    el.addEventListener("pointerup", up);
    el.addEventListener("pointercancel", cancel);
  }));
  return host;
}
// %%
engine = {
// Ordinal diagram engine. Pure functions; every iteration order is sorted so the output is a
// function of the input sets only (row order in the snapshot does not matter).

const cmp = (a, b) => {
  const ta = typeof a, tb = typeof b;
  if (ta !== tb) return ta === "number" ? -1 : tb === "number" ? 1 : ta < tb ? -1 : 1;
  return a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0;
};
const cmpTuple = (a, b) => {
  const n = Math.min(a.length, b.length);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const c = cmp(a[i], b[i]); if (c) return c; }
  return a.length - b.length;
};
const keyOf = (t) => JSON.stringify(t);
const isNil = (v) => v === null || v === undefined;

// --- fractional keys (Greenspan's midpoint, base 36, keys never end in "0") ---
const DIG = "0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz";
const midpoint = (a, b) => {
  if (b !== null) {
    let n = 0;
    while ((a[n] || "0") === b[n]) n++;
    if (n > 0) return b.slice(0, n) + midpoint(a.slice(n), b.slice(n));
  }
  const da = a ? DIG.indexOf(a[0]) : 0;
  const db = b !== null ? DIG.indexOf(b[0]) : DIG.length;
  if (db - da > 1) return DIG[Math.floor((da + db) / 2)];
  if (b !== null && b.length > 1) return b.slice(0, 1);
  return DIG[da] + midpoint(a.slice(1), null);
};
const keyBetween = (a, b) => midpoint(a || "", isNil(b) ? null : b);

// --- poset level: SCC condensation, then longest path from sources ---
const posetRanks = (ids, edges) => {
  const idSet = new Set(ids);
  const out = new Map(ids.map((id) => [id, []]));
  for (const e of edges) if (idSet.has(e.src) && idSet.has(e.dst) && e.src !== e.dst) out.get(e.src).push(e.dst);
  for (const l of out.values()) l.sort(cmp);
  // Tarjan, iterative, visiting ids in sorted order.
  let index = 0;
  const idx = new Map(), low = new Map(), onStack = new Set(), stack = [], comp = new Map();
  for (const root of ids) {
    if (idx.has(root)) continue;
    const work = [[root, 0]];
    idx.set(root, index); low.set(root, index); index++; stack.push(root); onStack.add(root);
    while (work.length) {
      const top = work[work.length - 1];
      const [v, i] = top;
      const succ = out.get(v);
      if (i < succ.length) {
        top[1]++;
        const w = succ[i];
        if (!idx.has(w)) {
          idx.set(w, index); low.set(w, index); index++; stack.push(w); onStack.add(w);
          work.push([w, 0]);
        } else if (onStack.has(w)) low.set(v, Math.min(low.get(v), idx.get(w)));
      } else {
        work.pop();
        if (work.length) { const p = work[work.length - 1][0]; low.set(p, Math.min(low.get(p), low.get(v))); }
        if (low.get(v) === idx.get(v)) {
          const members = [];
          let w;
          do { w = stack.pop(); onStack.delete(w); members.push(w); } while (w !== v);
          members.sort(cmp);
          for (const m of members) comp.set(m, members[0]);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const comps = [...new Set(ids.map((id) => comp.get(id)))].sort(cmp);
  const cout = new Map(comps.map((c) => [c, new Set()]));
  const indeg = new Map(comps.map((c) => [c, 0]));
  for (const [v, l] of out) for (const w of l) {
    const a = comp.get(v), b = comp.get(w);
    if (a !== b && !cout.get(a).has(b)) { cout.get(a).add(b); indeg.set(b, indeg.get(b) + 1); }
  }
  const rank = new Map(comps.map((c) => [c, 0]));
  let ready = comps.filter((c) => indeg.get(c) === 0);
  while (ready.length) {
    const c = ready.shift();
    for (const d of [...cout.get(c)].sort(cmp)) {
      rank.set(d, Math.max(rank.get(d), rank.get(c) + 1));
      indeg.set(d, indeg.get(d) - 1);
      if (indeg.get(d) === 0) { ready.push(d); ready.sort(cmp); }
    }
  }
  const byComp = new Map();
  for (const id of ids) { const c = comp.get(id); if (!byComp.has(c)) byComp.set(c, []); byComp.get(c).push(id); }
  const sccs = [...byComp.values()].filter((m) => m.length > 1).map((m) => m.sort(cmp)).sort((a, b) => cmp(a[0], b[0]));
  return { rank: new Map(ids.map((id) => [id, rank.get(comp.get(id))])), sccs };
};

// --- layout ---
// view: { y: [level], x: [level], drawRelations?: [rel], hulls?: false, wrap?: boxes per line in a cell (6), kinds?: [kind] shown }
// node: { id, label?, kind?, href?, ...columns }; edge: { src, dst, rel, prov? } with prov data | docs | inferred
// level: { col, label? } (total order on a column) or { relation, by?, label? } (poset rank along edges of that relation;
// with by, the rank of the node's value in column by, edges first lifted to that column).
// order: [{ id, fkey }] human scale. folds on the y axis: a prefix tuple folds that prefix; a number k folds every
// prefix of length k; { open: prefix } keeps one prefix open under a number. view.cellSort: columns ordering a cell before fkey.
const layout = ({ view, nodes, edges = [], hulls = [], order = [], folds = [] }) => {
  const levelsOf = (axis) => view[axis] || [];
  // filter: { col: [allowed values] }; a missing value is matched as "∅". kinds is filter.kind.
  const filter = Object.entries({ ...(view.kinds ? { kind: view.kinds } : {}), ...(view.filter || {}) }).filter(([, v]) => v).map(([c, v]) => [c, new Set(v.map(String))]);
  const all = nodes.filter((n) => filter.every(([c, ok]) => ok.has(isNil(n[c]) ? "∅" : String(n[c])))).sort((a, b) => cmp(a.id, b.id));
  const included = [], excluded = [];
  for (const n of all) {
    const missing = [...levelsOf("y"), ...levelsOf("x")].some((l) => l.col && isNil(n[l.col]));
    (missing ? excluded : included).push(n);
  }
  const ids = included.map((n) => n.id);
  const byId = new Map(included.map((n) => [n.id, n]));
  const sortedEdges = [...edges].sort((a, b) => cmp(a.src, b.src) || cmp(a.dst, b.dst) || cmp(a.rel, b.rel));
  const ranks = new Map(), sccs = [];
  const rankKey = (l) => l.relation + (l.by ? "\u0000" + l.by : "");
  for (const l of [...levelsOf("y"), ...levelsOf("x")]) if (l.relation && !ranks.has(rankKey(l))) {
    const of = l.by ? (id) => byId.get(id)[l.by] : (id) => id;
    const units = [...new Set(ids.map(of))].sort(cmp);
    const rel = sortedEdges.filter((e) => e.rel === l.relation && byId.has(e.src) && byId.has(e.dst)).map((e) => ({ src: of(e.src), dst: of(e.dst) }));
    const r = posetRanks(units, rel);
    ranks.set(rankKey(l), new Map(ids.map((id) => [id, r.rank.get(of(id))])));
    for (const s of r.sccs) sccs.push({ relation: l.relation, members: s });
  }
  const val = (n, l) => (l.relation ? ranks.get(rankKey(l)).get(n.id) : n[l.col]);
  const path = (n, axis) => levelsOf(axis).map((l) => val(n, l));
  const fkey = new Map(order.map((o) => [o.id, o.fkey]));
  const tie = (n) => [...(view.cellSort || []).map((c) => (isNil(n[c]) ? "~" : n[c])), fkey.has(n.id) ? fkey.get(n.id) : "~", n.id];

  const foldSet = new Set(folds.filter(Array.isArray).map(keyOf));
  const foldDepths = new Set(folds.filter(Number.isInteger));
  const openSet = new Set(folds.filter((f) => f && f.open).map((f) => keyOf(f.open)));
  const isFolded = (p) => foldSet.has(keyOf(p)) || (foldDepths.has(p.length) && !openSet.has(keyOf(p)));
  const groupOf = new Map();
  for (const n of included) {
    const yp = path(n, "y");
    for (let k = 1; k <= yp.length; k++) if (isFolded(yp.slice(0, k))) { groupOf.set(n.id, keyOf(yp.slice(0, k))); break; }
  }
  const cols = [...new Map(included.map((n) => [keyOf(path(n, "x")), path(n, "x")])).values()].sort(cmpTuple);
  const colIndex = new Map(cols.map((c, i) => [keyOf(c), i]));
  const colOf = (n) => colIndex.get(keyOf(path(n, "x")));
  const groups = new Map();
  for (const n of included) if (groupOf.has(n.id)) {
    const g = groupOf.get(n.id);
    if (!groups.has(g)) groups.set(g, []);
    groups.get(g).push(n);
  }
  // view.cards: a folded prefix whose members share one column is drawn as a box in its parent's row,
  // beside that row's other boxes, instead of as a bar on a row of its own.
  const card = new Set([...groups].filter(([g, m]) => view.cards && JSON.parse(g).length > 0 && new Set(m.map(colOf)).size === 1).map(([g]) => g));
  const rowOf = new Map();
  for (const n of included) {
    const g = groupOf.get(n.id);
    rowOf.set(n.id, !g ? path(n, "y") : card.has(g) ? JSON.parse(g).slice(0, -1) : JSON.parse(g));
  }
  const rows = [...new Map(included.map((n) => [keyOf(rowOf.get(n.id)), rowOf.get(n.id)])).values()].sort(cmpTuple);
  const rowIndex = new Map(rows.map((r, i) => [keyOf(r), i]));

  const kindsOf = (members) => {
    const byKind = new Map();
    for (const m of members) byKind.set(m.kind ?? "", (byKind.get(m.kind ?? "") || 0) + 1);
    return [...byKind].sort((a, b) => cmp(a[0], b[0])).map(([kind, n]) => ({ kind, n }));
  };
  const items = [];
  const cells = new Map(); // "r,c" -> ordered ids (a card by its group key)
  const entry = new Map(); // "r,c" -> [{ tie, leaf | card }]
  const put = (k, e) => { if (!entry.has(k)) entry.set(k, []); entry.get(k).push(e); };
  for (const n of included) if (!groupOf.has(n.id)) put(rowIndex.get(keyOf(rowOf.get(n.id))) + "," + colOf(n), { tie: tie(n), n });
  for (const g of card) {
    const members = groups.get(g);
    const first = [...members].sort((a, b) => cmpTuple(tie(a), tie(b)))[0];
    put(rowIndex.get(keyOf(rowOf.get(first.id))) + "," + colOf(first), { tie: tie(first), g, members });
  }
  const wrap = view.wrap || 6;
  const lines = rows.map(() => 1);
  const occupancy = new Map();
  const occ = (r, c, w) => { const k = r + "," + c; occupancy.set(k, Math.max(occupancy.get(k) || 0, w)); };
  for (const [k, list] of [...entry].sort((a, b) => cmp(a[0], b[0]))) {
    list.sort((a, b) => cmpTuple(a.tie, b.tie));
    const [r, c] = k.split(",").map(Number);
    list.forEach((e, slot) => items.push(e.n
      ? { kind: "leaf", key: e.n.id, id: e.n.id, row: r, col: c, slot, label: String(e.n.label ?? e.n.id), node: e.n }
      : { kind: "group", card: true, key: e.g, row: r, col: c, colMin: c, colMax: c, slot, members: e.members.map((m) => m.id), kinds: kindsOf(e.members), label: `${e.members.length} items` }));
    occ(r, c, Math.min(list.length, wrap));
    lines[r] = Math.max(lines[r], Math.ceil(list.length / wrap));
    cells.set(k, list.map((e) => (e.n ? e.n.id : e.g)));
  }
  for (const [g, members] of [...groups].sort((a, b) => cmp(a[0], b[0]))) {
    if (card.has(g)) continue;
    const cs = members.map(colOf);
    const colMin = Math.min(...cs), colMax = Math.max(...cs);
    const r = rowIndex.get(g);
    for (let c = colMin; c <= colMax; c++) occ(r, c, 1);
    items.push({ kind: "group", key: g, row: r, colMin, colMax, members: members.map((m) => m.id), kinds: kindsOf(members), label: `${members.length} items` });
  }
  const colWidth = cols.map((_, c) => Math.max(1, ...rows.map((_, r) => occupancy.get(r + "," + c) || 0)));
  const visible = new Map(included.map((n) => [n.id, groupOf.get(n.id) || n.id]));

  const lifted = new Map(), internal = new Map(), labels = new Map(), weights = new Map(), sources = new Map();
  const draw = view.drawRelations ? new Set(view.drawRelations) : null;
  for (const e of sortedEdges) {
    if (!byId.has(e.src) || !byId.has(e.dst) || (draw && !draw.has(e.rel))) continue;
    const s = visible.get(e.src), d = visible.get(e.dst);
    if (s === d) { internal.set(s, (internal.get(s) || 0) + (e.n ?? 1)); continue; }
    const k = keyOf([s, d, e.rel, e.prov || "data", e.state || null]);
    lifted.set(k, (lifted.get(k) || 0) + 1);
    // weight is the number of base rows behind the line: an input line that already merged n rows counts n.
    weights.set(k, (weights.get(k) || 0) + (e.n ?? 1));
    if (e.label) labels.set(k, [...(labels.get(k) || []), ...[].concat(e.label)]);
    if (e.pairs) sources.set(k, [...(sources.get(k) || []), ...e.pairs]);
  }
  const liftedEdges = [...lifted].sort((a, b) => cmp(a[0], b[0])).map(([k, count]) => {
    const [src, dst, rel, prov, state] = JSON.parse(k);
    return { src, dst, rel, prov, ...(state ? { state } : {}), count, weight: weights.get(k), labels: [...new Set(labels.get(k) || [])].sort(cmp), pairs: [...new Set(sources.get(k) || [])].sort(cmp) };
  });

  const hullMap = new Map();
  for (const h of view.hulls === false ? [] : [...hulls].sort((a, b) => cmp(a.hull, b.hull) || cmp(a.id, b.id))) {
    if (!byId.has(h.id)) continue;
    if (!hullMap.has(h.hull)) hullMap.set(h.hull, new Set());
    hullMap.get(h.hull).add(visible.get(h.id));
  }
  const hullList = [...hullMap].map(([hull, s]) => ({ hull, items: [...s].sort(cmp) }));

  return { rows, cols, colWidth, lines, wrap, items, cells, liftedEdges, internal, sccs, hulls: hullList, excluded: excluded.map((n) => n.id), included: ids, view, foldDepths: [...foldDepths].sort(cmp) };
};

// --- human scale: a drag inside a cell writes fkeys ---
// Returns the new order table and the rows written. Once every member of the cell has a key,
// a drag writes exactly one row.
const reorder = ({ order, cellIds, id, toIndex }) => {
  const fkey = new Map(order.map((o) => [o.id, o.fkey]));
  const rest = cellIds.filter((x) => x !== id);
  const at = Math.max(0, Math.min(toIndex, rest.length));
  let written;
  if (rest.every((x) => fkey.has(x))) {
    written = [{ id, fkey: keyBetween(at > 0 ? fkey.get(rest[at - 1]) : "", at < rest.length ? fkey.get(rest[at]) : null) }];
  } else {
    const seq = [...rest.slice(0, at), id, ...rest.slice(at)];
    let prev = "";
    written = seq.map((x) => { prev = keyBetween(prev, null); return { id: x, fkey: prev }; });
  }
  const changed = new Set(written.map((w) => w.id));
  const next = [...order.filter((o) => !changed.has(o.id)), ...written].sort((a, b) => cmp(a.id, b.id));
  return { order: next, written };
};

// --- geometry + SVG ---
const SHOW_MAX = 40;
// Extra text lines on a leaf box: one per shown column, or one per item of a list column.
const showLinesOf = (view, node) => (view.show || []).reduce((sum, c) => {
  const v = node[c];
  return sum + (Array.isArray(v) ? Math.max(1, Math.min(v.length, SHOW_MAX) + (v.length > SHOW_MAX ? 1 : 0)) : 1);
}, 0);
const geometry = (L, { slot = 118, gap = 26, rowH = 46, boxH = 26, levelW = 118, top = 30 } = {}) => {
  // A box is as tall as its own text; a row line is as tall as the tallest box in that row. Fold bars keep 26 px.
  slot = L.view.slot || slot;
  const extraOf = (it) => (it.kind === "leaf" ? 13 * showLinesOf(L.view, it.node) : it.card ? 13 : 0);
  const unit = L.rows.map(() => rowH);
  for (const it of L.items) unit[it.row] = Math.max(unit[it.row], rowH + extraOf(it));
  const gutter = levelW * Math.max(1, L.view.y.length);
  const colX = [];
  let x = gutter + 16;
  L.colWidth.forEach((w, c) => { colX[c] = x; x += w * slot + gap; });
  const width = x;
  const lines = L.lines || L.rows.map(() => 1), wrap = L.wrap || Infinity;
  const rowTop = [top];
  lines.forEach((n, r) => rowTop.push(rowTop[r] + n * unit[r]));
  const rowY = (r) => rowTop[r];
  const rowHeight = (r) => lines[r] * unit[r];
  const pad = (rowH - boxH) / 2;
  const box = new Map();
  for (const it of L.items) {
    if (it.kind === "leaf" || it.card) box.set(it.key, { x: colX[it.col] + (it.slot % wrap) * slot, y: rowY(it.row) + pad + Math.floor(it.slot / wrap) * unit[it.row], w: slot - 12, h: boxH + extraOf(it) });
    else box.set(it.key, { x: colX[it.colMin], y: rowY(it.row) + pad, w: colX[it.colMax] + L.colWidth[it.colMax] * slot - 12 - colX[it.colMin], h: boxH });
  }
  return { gutter, colX, width, height: rowY(L.rows.length) + 24, rowY, rowHeight, box, slot, rowH, levelW, top };
};

const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;").replace(/"/g, "&quot;");
const f1 = (v) => Math.round(v * 10) / 10;
const clip = (s, n) => (s.length > n ? s.slice(0, n - 1) + "…" : s);
const KIND_FILL = ["#ffffff", "#fef3c7", "#dcfce7", "#ede9fe", "#fee2e2", "#e0f2fe"];
const DASH = { docs: "5 3", inferred: "1.5 3" };
// A compared line: in both, observed only, claimed only (Murphy, Notkin, Sullivan 1995).
const STATE = { convergence: "#6b7280", divergence: "#d97706", absence: "#dc2626" };

const convexHull = (pts) => {
  const p = [...pts].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);
  if (p.length < 3) return p;
  const cross = (o, a, b) => (a[0] - o[0]) * (b[1] - o[1]) - (a[1] - o[1]) * (b[0] - o[0]);
  const lo = [], hi = [];
  for (const q of p) { while (lo.length >= 2 && cross(lo[lo.length - 2], lo[lo.length - 1], q) <= 0) lo.pop(); lo.push(q); }
  for (const q of [...p].reverse()) { while (hi.length >= 2 && cross(hi[hi.length - 2], hi[hi.length - 1], q) <= 0) hi.pop(); hi.push(q); }
  return [...lo.slice(0, -1), ...hi.slice(0, -1)];
};

// off shifts a path sideways so two opposite edges between the same boxes stay apart.
// over arcs above the row, for an edge whose straight curve would pass behind another box.
const anchors = (a, b, off = 0, over = false, blocked = {}) => {
  const ac = a.x + a.w / 2, bc = b.x + b.w / 2;
  if (over) {
    const x1 = ac + off, x2 = bc + off, y = a.y;
    const lift = 16 + Math.abs(x2 - x1) * 0.12;
    return `M${f1(x1)},${f1(y)} C${f1(x1)},${f1(y - lift)} ${f1(x2)},${f1(y - lift)} ${f1(x2)},${f1(y)}`;
  }
  const overlapX = a.x < b.x + b.w && b.x < a.x + a.w;
  if (overlapX || Math.abs(ac - bc) < 1) {
    const x1 = Math.min(Math.max(bc, a.x + 8), a.x + a.w - 8) + off, x2 = Math.min(Math.max(ac, b.x + 8), b.x + b.w - 8) + off;
    const down = b.y > a.y;
    const y1 = down ? a.y + a.h : a.y, y2 = down ? b.y : b.y + b.h;
    const dy = (y2 - y1) / 2;
    return `M${f1(x1)},${f1(y1)} C${f1(x1)},${f1(y1 + dy)} ${f1(x2)},${f1(y2 - dy)} ${f1(x2)},${f1(y2)}`;
  }
  const right = bc > ac, down = b.y > a.y;
  // An end whose row has a box between the two ends leaves or enters through its top or bottom.
  const p1 = blocked.src ? [ac + off, down ? a.y + a.h : a.y] : [right ? a.x + a.w : a.x, a.y + a.h / 2 + off];
  const p2 = blocked.dst ? [bc + off, down ? b.y : b.y + b.h] : [right ? b.x : b.x + b.w, b.y + b.h / 2 + off];
  const c1 = blocked.src ? [p1[0], (p1[1] + p2[1]) / 2] : [(p1[0] + p2[0]) / 2, p1[1]];
  const c2 = blocked.dst ? [p2[0], (p1[1] + p2[1]) / 2] : [(p1[0] + p2[0]) / 2, p2[1]];
  return `M${f1(p1[0])},${f1(p1[1])} C${f1(c1[0])},${f1(c1[1])} ${f1(c2[0])},${f1(c2[1])} ${f1(p2[0])},${f1(p2[1])}`;
};

// Gutter labels: one per distinct visible y-prefix, spanning the rows that start with it.
const gutterLabels = (L, labelFor) => {
  const out = [];
  const depth = L.view.y.length;
  for (let k = 1; k <= depth; k++) {
    let start = 0;
    for (let r = 0; r <= L.rows.length; r++) {
      const cur = r < L.rows.length && L.rows[r].length >= k ? keyOf(L.rows[r].slice(0, k)) : null;
      const prev = r > 0 && L.rows[r - 1].length >= k ? keyOf(L.rows[r - 1].slice(0, k)) : null;
      if (r > 0 && cur !== prev && prev !== null) out.push({ k, prefix: JSON.parse(prev), r0: start, r1: r - 1, folded: L.rows[r - 1].length === k && L.items.some((it) => it.kind === "group" && it.key === prev) });
      if (cur !== prev) start = r;
    }
  }
  return out.map((g) => ({ ...g, text: labelFor(g.prefix) }));
};

const render = (L, opts = {}) => {
  const G = geometry(L, opts);
  const kinds = [...new Set(L.items.filter((it) => it.kind === "leaf" && it.node.kind).map((it) => it.node.kind))].sort(cmp);
  const labelFor = opts.labelFor || ((p) => String(p[p.length - 1]));
  const parts = [];
  parts.push(`<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 ${f1(G.width)} ${f1(G.height)}" width="${f1(G.width)}" height="${f1(G.height)}" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" class="odg">`);
  // Arrowheads in user units, so a wide line does not get a wide head; one per line colour.
  const arrows = Object.entries({ "": "#6b7280", ...STATE }).map(([k, c]) => `<marker id="odg-arrow${k ? "-" + k : ""}" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="${c}"/></marker>`);
  parts.push(`<defs>${arrows.join("")}</defs>`);
  L.rows.forEach((_, r) => { if (r % 2 === 0) parts.push(`<rect x="0" y="${f1(G.rowY(r))}" width="${f1(G.width)}" height="${G.rowHeight(r)}" fill="#000" fill-opacity="0.035"/>`); });
  const chars = Math.floor((G.slot - 26) / 5.6);
  const showText = (n) => (L.view.show || []).flatMap((c) => {
    const v = n[c];
    // view.showNames false prints the value alone, for a column whose values say what they are, and nothing when there is none.
    if (L.view.showNames === false && isNil(v)) return [];
    if (!Array.isArray(v)) return [`${L.view.showNames === false ? "" : c + " "}${isNil(v) ? "∅" : v}`];
    if (!v.length) return [`${c}: none`];
    return [...v.slice(0, SHOW_MAX), ...(v.length > SHOW_MAX ? [`… ${v.length - SHOW_MAX} more`] : [])];
  });
  const shows = (n, b) => showText(n).map((t, i) => `<text x="${f1(b.x + 7)}" y="${f1(b.y + 30 + 13 * i)}" fill="#6b7280" font-size="10">${esc(clip(t, chars))}</text>`).join("");
  // "12 methods, 1 worker"; a group of rows with no kind is its count alone.
  const counts = (it) => (it.kinds.every((k) => k.kind) ? [...it.kinds].sort((x, y) => y.n - x.n || cmp(x.kind, y.kind)).map((k) => `${k.n} ${k.n === 1 ? k.kind.replace(/s$/, "") : k.kind.replace(/s?$/, "s")}`).join(", ") : String(it.members.length));
  const xLabelFor = opts.xLabelFor || ((c) => (L.view.xTitle || "x") + " " + c.join(" · "));
  if (L.view.x && L.view.x.length) L.cols.forEach((c, i) => parts.push(`<text x="${f1(G.colX[i])}" y="${G.top - 10}" fill="#6b7280">${esc(xLabelFor(c))}</text>`));
  // One header per y level: a click folds or opens every prefix of that length.
  L.view.y.forEach((l, i) => {
    const folded = (L.foldDepths || []).includes(i + 1);
    parts.push(`<g class="odg-fold" data-fold="${i + 1}" style="cursor:pointer"><text x="${i * G.levelW + 6}" y="${G.top - 10}" fill="#6b7280" font-weight="600">${esc(clip(`${folded ? "▸" : "▾"} ${l.col || "depth along " + l.relation}`, Math.floor(G.levelW / 6.2)))}<title>${esc(l.col || "depth along " + l.relation)}</title></text></g>`);
  });
  for (const g of gutterLabels(L, labelFor)) {
    const y0 = G.rowY(g.r0), y1 = G.rowY(g.r1 + 1);
    const x = (g.k - 1) * G.levelW + 6;
    parts.push(`<g class="odg-fold" data-fold="${esc(keyOf(g.prefix))}" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="${x - 4}" y="${f1(y0 + 3)}" width="${G.levelW - 6}" height="${f1(y1 - y0 - 6)}" rx="4" fill="#3b82f6" fill-opacity="0.07"/><text x="${x}" y="${f1(y0 + 18)}" fill="#1f2937">${g.folded ? "▸" : "▾"} ${esc(g.text)}</text></g>`);
  }
  const hullColors = ["#f59e0b", "#10b981", "#8b5cf6", "#ef4444"];
  L.hulls.forEach((h, i) => {
    const pts = [];
    for (const k of h.items) { const b = G.box.get(k); pts.push([b.x, b.y], [b.x + b.w, b.y], [b.x, b.y + b.h], [b.x + b.w, b.y + b.h]); }
    const hp = convexHull(pts);
    const c = hullColors[i % hullColors.length];
    parts.push(`<path class="odg-hull" data-hull="${esc(h.hull)}" d="M${hp.map((p) => f1(p[0]) + "," + f1(p[1])).join(" L")} Z" fill="${c}" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke="${c}" stroke-opacity="0.35" stroke-width="16" stroke-linejoin="round"/>`);
    const lx = Math.min(...hp.map((p) => p[0])), ly = Math.min(...hp.map((p) => p[1]));
    parts.push(`<text x="${f1(lx - 4)}" y="${f1(ly - 10)}" fill="${c}" font-weight="600">${esc(h.hull)}</text>`);
  });
  // A cycle with a member folded away shows as two-way lifted edges instead of an outline.
  // One outline per member: a bounding box would cover other boxes once a cell wraps.
  for (const s of L.sccs.filter((c) => c.members.every((m) => G.box.has(m)))) {
    for (const m of s.members) {
      const b = G.box.get(m);
      parts.push(`<rect class="odg-scc" data-relation="${esc(s.relation)}" data-members="${esc(s.members.join(" "))}" x="${f1(b.x - 4)}" y="${f1(b.y - 4)}" width="${f1(b.w + 8)}" height="${f1(b.h + 8)}" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>`);
    }
  }
  const pairs = new Set(L.liftedEdges.map((e) => e.src + "\u0000" + e.dst));
  const boxes = [...G.box.entries()];
  for (const e of L.liftedEdges) {
    const a = G.box.get(e.src), b = G.box.get(e.dst);
    const off = pairs.has(e.dst + "\u0000" + e.src) ? (cmp(e.src, e.dst) < 0 ? 5 : -5) : 0;
    const lo = Math.min(a.x, b.x), hi = Math.max(a.x + a.w, b.x + b.w);
    const between = (row) => boxes.some(([k, c]) => k !== e.src && k !== e.dst && c.y === row && c.x > lo && c.x + c.w < hi);
    const over = a.y === b.y && between(a.y);
    const blocked = a.y === b.y ? {} : { src: between(a.y), dst: between(b.y) };
    parts.push(`<path class="odg-edge" d="${anchors(a, b, off, over, blocked)}" fill="none" stroke="${STATE[e.state] || "#6b7280"}" stroke-width="${f1(Math.min(5, 1.2 + Math.log2(e.weight)))}"${DASH[e.prov] ? ` stroke-dasharray="${DASH[e.prov]}"` : ""} data-rel="${esc(e.rel)}" data-prov="${esc(e.prov || "data")}"${e.state ? ` data-state="${e.state}"` : ""} marker-end="url(#odg-arrow${e.state ? "-" + e.state : ""})"><title>${esc([e.state, ...(e.pairs.length ? e.pairs : e.labels)].filter(Boolean).join("\n"))}</title></path>`);
    if (L.view.edgeLabels && e.labels.length) {
      const mx = 0.5 * (a.x + a.w / 2 + b.x + b.w / 2), my = over ? a.y - 16 - Math.abs(b.x - a.x) * 0.09 : 0.5 * (a.y + b.y) + a.h / 2;
      parts.push(`<text x="${f1(mx)}" y="${f1(my)}" fill="#4b5563" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#f6f7f9" stroke-width="3">${esc(clip(e.labels.join(", "), 28))}</text>`);
    }
    if (e.weight > 1) {
      // Near the arrowhead, so a count reads as belonging to its target.
      const mx = 0.25 * (a.x + a.w / 2) + 0.75 * (b.x + b.w / 2), my = over ? a.y - 18 - Math.abs(b.x - a.x) * 0.09 : 0.25 * a.y + 0.75 * b.y - (b.y > a.y ? 4 : -a.h - 10);
      parts.push(`<text x="${f1(mx + (off < 0 ? -14 : 14))}" y="${f1(my)}" fill="#374151" text-anchor="middle" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#f6f7f9" stroke-width="3">×${e.weight}</text>`);
    }
  }
  for (const it of L.items) {
    const b = G.box.get(it.key);
    const inner = L.internal.get(it.key);
    if (it.kind === "leaf") {
      const kind = it.node.kind, fill = kind ? KIND_FILL[kinds.indexOf(kind) % KIND_FILL.length] : "#fff";
      const link = it.node.href ? `<a href="${esc(it.node.href)}" target="_blank" class="odg-link"><rect x="${f1(b.x + b.w - 16)}" y="${f1(b.y + 1)}" width="15" height="24" fill="#000" fill-opacity="0"/><text x="${f1(b.x + b.w - 13)}" y="${f1(b.y + 17)}" fill="#2563eb">↗</text></a>` : "";
      parts.push(`<g class="odg-node" data-id="${esc(it.id)}"${kind ? ` data-kind="${esc(kind)}"` : ""} style="cursor:grab"><rect x="${f1(b.x)}" y="${f1(b.y)}" width="${f1(b.w)}" height="${b.h}" rx="4" fill="${fill}" stroke="#9ca3af"/><text x="${f1(b.x + 7)}" y="${f1(b.y + 17)}" fill="#111827">${esc(clip(it.label, Math.max(it.node.href ? 14 : 16, Math.floor((b.w - (it.node.href ? 24 : 10)) / 6.6))))}</text>${shows(it.node, b)}${link}</g>`);
    } else {
      // A card is a folded group in its parent's row: name, then its counts on a second line.
      const text = it.card
        ? `<text x="${f1(b.x + 10)}" y="${f1(b.y + 17)}" fill="#1e3a8a">${esc(clip(`▸ ${labelFor(JSON.parse(it.key))}`, Math.floor(b.w / 6.2)))}</text><text x="${f1(b.x + 10)}" y="${f1(b.y + 31)}" fill="#1e3a8a" font-size="10">${esc(clip(counts(it) + (inner ? ` · ${inner} inside` : ""), Math.floor(b.w / 5.4)))}</text>`
        : `<text x="${f1(b.x + 10)}" y="${f1(b.y + 17)}" fill="#1e3a8a">${esc(clip(`▸ ${labelFor(JSON.parse(it.key))} · ${counts(it)}${inner ? ` · ${inner} inside` : ""}`, Math.floor(b.w / 5.8)))}</text>`;
      parts.push(`<g class="odg-group" data-fold="${esc(it.key)}" data-members="${esc(it.members.join(" "))}" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="${f1(b.x)}" y="${f1(b.y)}" width="${f1(b.w)}" height="${b.h}" rx="${it.card ? 6 : 13}" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6"/>${text}</g>`);
    }
  }
  parts.push(`</svg>`);
  return { svg: parts.join("\n"), geometry: G };
};
  return { cmp, cmpTuple, keyBetween, posetRanks, layout, reorder, geometry, render, convexHull };
}
// %%
md`## The spec

For the person who builds the module.`
// %%
viewof specStatus = sticky(Inputs.select(["draft", "in review", "approved for handover"], { label: "Status", value: "draft" }), "draft")
// %%
readiness = {
  const notes = (annotations || []).filter((a) => a.home === specModule || (a.anchor && a.anchor.module === specModule));
  const unchecked = requirements.filter((r) => !r.check || /^<.*>$/.test(r.check.trim()));
  const blocking = questions.filter((q) => q.blocking && !q.answer);
  const undrawn = states.filter((s) => !s.drawing);
  const items = [
    [notes.length, "annotations to resolve"],
    [blocking.length, "blocking questions open"],
    [unchecked.length, `of ${requirements.length} requirements without a check`],
    [undrawn.length, `of ${states.length} states without a drawing`]
  ];
  const ready = items.every(([n]) => n === 0) && specStatus === "approved for handover";
  // Everything that still needs the reviewer, listed here with a link to where it is answered.
  const open = questions.map((q, i) => ({ q, i })).filter(({ q }) => !q.answer);
  const todo = [
    ...open.filter(({ q }) => q.blocking).map(({ q, i }) => ({ tag: "blocking question", text: q.q, to: `[data-question="${i}"]` })),
    ...open.filter(({ q }) => !q.blocking).map(({ q, i }) => ({ tag: "open question", text: q.q, to: `[data-question="${i}"]` })),
    ...unchecked.map((r) => ({ tag: "no check", text: `${r.id} ${r.text}`, to: `[data-requirement="${r.id}"]` })),
    ...undrawn.map((s) => ({ tag: "not drawn", text: `state: ${s.state}`, to: `[data-state="${s.state}"]` }))
  ];
  const box = htl.html`<div style="font:13px system-ui;padding:.5em .8em;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);border-radius:6px"></div>`;
  // Scrolls the pane; a plain #fragment link would replace the lopepage layout hash.
  const jump = (to) => (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const el = (box.closest(".lp2-pane") || box.ownerDocument).querySelector(to);
    if (!el) return;
    el.scrollIntoView({ block: "center", behavior: "smooth" });
    if (el.animate) el.animate([{ background: "color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent)" }, { background: "transparent" }], 1800);
  };
  const short = (s) => (s.length > 110 ? s.slice(0, 110) + "…" : s);
  box.append(htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:1.2em;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline">
    <strong>${ready ? "Ready to hand over" : "Not ready to hand over"}</strong>
    ${items.map(([n, label]) => htl.html`<span style=${{ opacity: n ? 1 : 0.5 }}><strong>${n}</strong> ${label}</span>`)}
  </div>`);
  if (todo.length) box.append(htl.html`<ol style="margin:.5em 0 0;padding-left:1.4em">${todo.map((t) => htl.html`<li><a href="#" onclick=${jump(t.to)}>${t.tag}</a>: ${short(t.text)}</li>`)}</ol>`);
  return box;
}
// %%
md`## Reviewing this spec

- **Leave a note**: ☰ → Annotate → Note, then drag over the words or click the shape. Notes are review comments; Claude Code works through them, and you delete each when it is dealt with.
- **Ask about a spot**: ☰ → Annotate → Ask, then pick the words or shape and type. The answer threads at that spot.
- **Click prose** to rewrite it. **Drag shapes** in a drawing to move them.
- **Play with the prototype**: click a label in its left margin to fold or unfold that level; drag a box sideways to reorder it inside its cell.
- ☰ → **Save in place** keeps your edits and notes in this file.`
// %%
md`## Problem

Tom, 2026-10-25: "I think a diagram should be something close to an ontology. So the links and nodes map to something real, but we don't want a diagram to show everything, rather it has views, and the concept of expansions and compaction, like a 'details' but it folds elements up, so you can have a high level and/or a focus of a real system. The axis need to mean something ordinal, like Y is time, or Y is complexity."

Drawn diagrams (svg-lens, mermaid-lens in this corpus) store coordinates. A box placed by hand says nothing about the system, goes stale when the system changes, and there is no way to ask for the same picture one level up.`
// %%
md`## Outcome

- Given a snapshot (a named map of arrays of fixed-shape rows) and a view (which rows are boxes and lines, plus a level list per axis), the diagram is drawn with no hand placement.
- The same snapshot, view, folds and overlay give a byte-identical SVG, whatever order the snapshot rows arrive in.
- One snapshot is drawn through several views at once (step 11; the cb4 chapters), each with its own folds and order; hovering a box highlights the same row in every view.
- Clicking a level label folds every row under it into one span bar; edges crossing the fold are lifted onto the bar with a count.
- Dragging a box reorders it inside its cell by writing a fractional key to the overlay table; the snapshot tables are not modified.
- Rows with no value for an axis level are left out and counted.`
// %%
md`### Size

Not estimated. The engine above (layout, poset ranks, fold, lift, fractional keys, SVG) is 420 lines (\`engine.js\`, 2026-11-02, after nested folds and cards were added), plus 228 for reading tables into boxes and lines (\`rel.js\`, 2026-11-04), and was first written and tested in one session on 2026-10-26. A module with the open questions settled is more than that.`
// %%
md`## Scope

### Not your concern, do not build it

- Live data from the Cloud Brain or any endpoint. The input is a snapshot.
- A schema or vocabulary for architecture (service, store, calls…). The tool is schema-agnostic.
- Freehand drawing; that is svg-lens.
- Mermaid output; that is mermaid-lens.
- Editing the snapshot from the diagram.

### Non-goals

- Numeric axes. Levels are ordinal so they can fold; a numeric scale cannot collapse.
- A force-directed or optimising solver. The layout must be deterministic (Tom, 2026-10-26), and the ordinal levels leave nothing continuous to optimise.
- Edge routing around boxes. Edges are drawn as curves between box sides.`
// %%
md`## Words

The implementer uses these strings as written.`
// %%
copy_title = md`Ordinal diagram`
// %%
copy_opening = md`Each box is a row and each line is a row. Position comes from the axes you pick; folding a level gathers its rows into one bar. Dragging only reorders ties.`
// %%
copy_strings = md`| where | text |
|---|---|
| excluded notice | *N* rows have no value for this view's axes and are not drawn (*ids*) (one: "1 row has … and is not drawn") |
| folded group | ▸ *label* · *count*, or with kinds: ▸ *label* · *n* *kind*s, *m* *kind*s |
| folded card (second line) | *n* *kind*s, *m* *kind*s |
| folded group with internal edges | ▸ *label* · *count* · *k* inside |
| lifted edge with more than one | ×*count* |
| cycle outline tooltip | these rows reach each other along *relation*, so they share a rank |
| margin hint | click a label to fold or unfold it · drag a box sideways to reorder it (the tutorial steps use a hint per step instead) |`
// %%
md`### Tests

- On the 2026-10-27 snapshot (\`snapshot\`, \`snapshotSchema\`, \`views\`): views_differ, matrix_draws_no_edges, deterministic, excluded, cycle, fold_lift, drag_writes_one_row.
- On saved data: \`test_brain_fixture\` and \`test_strangers\` (cb4, 2026-10-31, test names 2026-11-04), \`test_tutorial_steps\` and \`test_hull\` (the web shop), \`test_compare\` (the web shop's design doc, and cb4's claims).`
// %%
