md`### Visual constraints

The prototype uses fixed light colours on a light panel (\`#f6f7f9\`) so it reads on the dark theme; a module should take theme variables instead. Slot 118 px, row 46 px, box 26 px, margin 118 px a y-level. At 640 px, chapter 3 (4 columns, cells wrapped at 3) scrolls horizontally inside its panel.`
// %%
md`## Behaviour

One requirement per row, in priority order.`
// %%
requirements = [
  { id: "R1", text: "The same snapshot, view, folds and overlay shall produce a byte-identical SVG, whatever order the snapshot rows are in.", check: "test_deterministic; bun test tools/scratch/ordinal-diagram/engine.test.js (shuffles with 3 seeds)" },
  { id: "R2", text: "Each axis shall be an ordered list of levels; a level is a column (total order) or a relation (rank along its edges); the human key and then id are always the last two levels.", check: "test_cycle; step 4: api.list and api.save share a cell, ordered by id" },
  { id: "R3", text: "When a y-prefix is folded, all rows under it shall draw as one bar spanning its members' columns (or, with view.cards and all members in one column, as one card in its parent's row), and edges with one end inside shall be lifted onto it with a count.", check: "test_fold_lift; step 7: click public edge and see one bar, ×2 from web.page" },
  { id: "R4", text: "A drag inside a cell shall write fractional keys to the overlay table and nothing else; once the cell is keyed, a drag writes one row.", check: "test_drag_writes_one_row; step 8: drag api.save left of api.list and see the order table gain 2 rows" },
  { id: "R5", text: "A row with no value for an axis column level shall be left out and counted under the diagram.", check: "test_excluded; step 9 names cache.get under its diagram" },
  { id: "R6", text: "Rows that reach each other along a rank relation shall share one rank and be outlined.", check: "test_cycle, test_brain_fixture; chapter 3 outlines fly and loop" },
  { id: "R7", text: "Rows of an n-ary table named as hulls shall be enclosed by one hull per key.", check: "test_hull; step 10: the save request hull encloses web.page, api.save, auth.check, db.write" },
  { id: "R8", text: "Boxes and lines shall be read from tables by their declared keys, with no query language and no node or edge table written by hand. Every diagram on the page is drawn this way.", check: "rel.test.js: every tutorial step, every chapter and the 2026-10-27 views lay out as the old hand-written rows did; test_tutorial_steps, test_brain_fixture" },
  { id: "R9", text: "Several views over one snapshot shall be drawn together, each with its own folds and order table, and hovering a box shall highlight the boxes holding the same row in every view.", check: "test_views_differ; step 11: fold serverless in the second view and the first is unchanged; hover a box and it is outlined orange in both" },
  { id: "R10", text: "A fold may name a whole y level, folding every prefix of that length, with single prefixes kept open; clicking a level's header toggles it, and a folded group's label counts its rows by kind.", check: "live.test.js 'methods inside their Worker'; Explore on cb4: click a card, then the nest 1 header" },
  { id: "R11", text: "A foreign key may name several tables (the first holding the key wins); a line lifted through a docs row is docs; lines with the same drawn ends are one line with the keys they end at; every key that names no row is listed.", check: "rel.test.js; chapter 5 dashes resources lines; Explore lists the keys that name no row (3 on live cb4, 2026-11-03)" },
  { id: "R12", text: "A view may compare a claimed relation with an observed one: after lifting, each pair of drawn ends gets one line, marked convergence (both), divergence (observed only) or absence (claimed only); with scope 'claimed', only divergences ending where a claim ends are kept.", check: "test_compare; rel.test.js 'the design doc against the calls', 'cb4's deployer reference claims four calls'; step 13 draws one red dashed web → auth" },
  { id: "R13", text: "Every line shall carry the base rows behind it; a fold's count and a line's width shall be the number of base rows, summed through every lift.", check: "rel.test.js 'a fold's line weight counts base rows'; hover a line to list its rows" },
  { id: "R14", text: "A lifted line shall equal Holt's lift without its '- D - A' term: containment composed with the relation composed with containment's inverse, less the identity. A line between a box and a box nested in it is kept (see Decisions).", check: "rel.test.js 'a lifted line is the relation composed with containment', on the shop and on cb4" }
]
// %%
requirementsTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th>id</th><th>requirement</th><th>check</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${requirements.map((r) => htl.html`<tr data-requirement=${r.id}><td><strong>${r.id}</strong></td><td>${r.text}</td><td>${r.check ? htl.html`<code>${r.check}</code>` : htl.html`<em>none</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
